{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-18T12:39:05.302Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented repository-relative tool paths in status observations, all within scope.\n\n**`src/watcher/runner.ts`**\n- Added exported `relativizeToolSummary(summary, root = process.cwd())`:\n  - normalizes trailing separators on `root` (keeps bare `/`/`\\` intact, bails on empty),\n  - globally strips `${root}/` and `${root}\\`,\n  - collapses an exact-root match to `.` via a boundary lookahead so `/rootfoo` isn't mangled.\n- `computeTaskHeartbeatStats` now takes optional `projectRoot?: string` and stores `relativizeToolSummary(summary, projectRoot)` for tool summaries (omitting it falls back to `process.cwd()`).\n- `runTask`'s heartbeat timer passes `projectRoot` through.\n\n**`tests/runner-terminal-status.test.ts`**\n- 5 pure tests for `relativizeToolSummary` (root+separator stripping, trailing-separator normalization, cwd fallback, outside-root untouched, exact-root → `.`).\n- 3 `computeTaskHeartbeatStats` tests: relativizes an absolute summary while asserting the raw `events.jsonl` is preserved, cwd fallback, and status-row rendering with no leading slash.\n- 1 end-to-end TTY test using a fake OpenCode binary emitting an absolute path, verifying the `runTask` plumbing.\n\n**Verification:** task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/runner-terminal-status.test.ts` → **25 pass / 0 fail**; `pnpm tsc --noEmit` and `pnpm lint` clean. Full suite has 3 pre-existing failures (task 2/3 regressions in `runner-already-running.test.ts` and `watcher-heartbeat.test.ts`) that are out of scope and documented in the result file."}}
